<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-BORDER TAKE LEAD OF 255 INTO FINAL DAY.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-BORDER TAKE LEAD OF 255 INTO FINAL DAY.</headline>
<dateline>EAST LONDON 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Border will take a lead of</p>
<p>255 runs into the final day of their Supersport series match</p>
<p>against Boland at Buffalo Park on Monday.</p>
<p>At close of play on Sunday Border were 201 for four in their</p>
<p>second innings having earlier dismissed Boland for 277.</p>
<p>Boland had resumed on 194 for four but lost their last five</p>
<p>wickets for a mere 41 runs as they battled against Peter</p>
<p>Emslie's off-spin. Emslie took three for 36.</p>
<p>Wayne Truter top scored with 95, including 10 fours, and</p>
<p>Andrew Wylie pitched in with 74.</p>
<p>The brightest batting of the Border innings came from Mark</p>
<p>Boucher (68 not out) and Vasbert Drakes (21 not out) who put on</p>
<p>61 in 36 minutes for the unbroken fifth wicket.</p>
<p>Scoreboard:</p>
<p>Border first innings 331 (Steven Pope 103, Pieter Strydom</p>
<p>100, Henry Williams 4-74)</p>
